  "articleBody": "Start by defining how the new level should function, then have the existing home and property reviewed before design decisions become expensive revisions. A successful second-story project typically moves through feasibility, measured design, structural planning, permit submittal, construction, inspections, and closeout, with scope and responsibilities documented at each stage.",
